course: dictionary
lesson: 9177
title: Small word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «So» is a tiny word with lots of jobs. Its main job is to show a reason and its result. «It rained, so we stayed in.» The rain is the reason, and staying in is what happened because of it.
explain: «So» can also make a word stronger, meaning very or very much. «I'm so happy!» Nothing is being joined here. The word just adds strength to happy, like a volume knob turned up.
explain: Use the clues around the word to choose its meaning. «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.» The second part is the result of the first, so this so means and that is why. Try swapping in therefore. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «So» links a reason to its result: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds, so only an adult uses it.»
fact: «So that» gives a purpose: «so that it never happens again» means the aim is to stop it happening.
fact: «So» can mean very: «I'm so happy!»
fact: «So» can also mean in this way or also: «I think so.» «So do I.»
fact: Formal writing often swaps «so» for «therefore», «hence» or «thus», and in maths and science «so» shows the next step or the cause and effect.
exercise: «Carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket, so even a small rise warms the planet.» What does so mean here? | Very, very much | Please stop | In this way, also | * And that is why
exercise: «Speak up so that we can hear.» What does «so that» give? | A rhyme | A question | * A purpose: the reason you speak up
exercise: «I'm so happy!» What does so mean? | In this way, also | * Very, very much | And that is why | Hence, thus, therefore
test: «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies, so the pressure does not crush them.» Which word could replace so here? | Very | * Therefore | Sadly | Blue
test: Mia says, «I think so.» What does so mean in that sentence? | Ten or more | * In this way, that is right | Very much | Next, in a line
exam: «The black box was found, so investigators could learn why the crash happened.» Which formal word could replace so? | Happily | Pink | Very | * Hence
